# Cloudflare Workers static-asset headers (honored from the deployed asset dir).
# The framework default for built assets is `max-age=0, must-revalidate`, which
# makes every navigation revalidate even content-hashed files. These rules give
# fingerprinted output a long immutable cache and the unhashed static files a
# long (mutable) cache, so repeat visits and same-session navigations skip the
# revalidation round-trip. The HTML documents are served by the Worker, not as
# static assets, so they are unaffected and stay fresh.
#
# `X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff` is repeated on EVERY rule, plus a catch-all `/*`
# at the bottom for the files no other rule names (robots.txt, humans.txt,
# manifest.webmanifest, the platform verification file). Static assets are served by
# Cloudflare's asset server and never reach the Worker — /llms.txt is the one
# worker-first exception (wrangler.jsonc) — so the Worker's security-header layer
# (src/lib/server/security-headers.ts) cannot stamp them, and this file is the only
# place that can. It is spelled out per rule rather than relying on a single `/*`
# because Cloudflare does not document whether several matching rules MERGE or whether
# the first match wins; written this way the caching above is untouched and the header
# lands under either reading.

# Content-hashed build output (e.g. /assets/index-CkMwHc4n.css): the hash in the
# filename changes whenever the bytes change, so these are safe to freeze.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Self-hosted fonts are named per-face and only change when the face changes.
/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Galaxy game sprite/audio assets.
/galaxy/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Brand/cover imagery and icons (unhashed names): cache for a week so they stop
# revalidating on every load, while still rolling over within a reasonable window.
# Paths must begin with `/`; the leading `*` splat matches any directory depth.
/*.webp
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
/*.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
/*.jpg
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
/*.ico
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=604800
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff

# Everything else in the asset dir: nosniff only, no caching opinion. Last so that
# under a first-match-wins reading it can never shadow a Cache-Control rule above.
/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
